# gitea-mirror naxsi whitelist - hand-written, NOT a community-maintained
# ruleset (none exists for gitea-mirror). Scoped narrowly to fix
# confirmed false positives from real traffic in naxsi_error.log; only
# extend when a new false positive is confirmed there, not speculatively.

# Preventive (not log-confirmed): a WAF should never content-scan a
# password field - assuming a standard "password" field name for this
# app's own login, same reasoning as the other password-field fixes.
# Confirm/adjust the field name if a login block still shows up in
# naxsi_error.log after this.
BasicRule wl:0 "mz:$BODY_VAR:password";

# Preventive: session cookies with heavily percent-encoded tokens trip
# the "double encoding" rule (1315) in the Cookie header - confirmed
# happening on Nextcloud and CheckMK. Same fix, applied ahead of time.
BasicRule wl:1000,1001,1005,1007,1010,1011,1013,1100,1101,1200,1308,1309,1310,1311,1315 "mz:$HEADERS_VAR:cookie";
